<Base title="About | Jair M. Morales Magallon" description="Who Jair M. Morales Magallon is: a cybersecurity student at Universidad Tecnológica de Panamá who builds websites for people and occasions." page="about" scripts={["js/name-water.js"]}>
      <div class="wrap page-head">
        <p class="crumb">~/jair/about</p>
        <h1 data-intro>Security student, web builder.</h1>
        <p class="lead" data-intro>I study how systems are protected, and I build things for the web.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="wrap about-grid section-tight">
        <!-- HISTORIA: edita los parrafos libremente. -->
        <div class="prose" data-intro>
          <h2>The short version</h2>
          <p>I'm Jair M. Morales Magallon, a Cybersecurity student at Universidad Tecnológica de Panamá. Since July 2026 I also teach programming at Centro ¡Supérate! Fundación Alberto Motta in La Chorrera, and I build websites for myself and for other people.</p>
          <p>Most of what I build starts with a person or an occasion: a quinceañera that needed an invitation, a graduation gift, a Christmas greeting, a community project that needed a home online. I make pages in any style, from presentation letters and invitations to informational and fully functional sites.</p>

          <h2>How I got here</h2>
          <p>I started programming in the technology courses at Centro ¡Supérate!, and what began as a class quickly turned into the thing I wanted to do every day. Today I'm back there on the other side of the room, teaching programming, web development and digital skills to younger students.</p>
          <p>I chose cybersecurity after discovering it in class. It's one of the fastest-growing fields in tech, and the more I learned, the more I realized that building something and protecting it are two halves of the same job. I'm now studying it at the Universidad Tecnológica de Panamá.</p>

          <h2>What motivates me</h2>
          <p>My goal is secure web development: building sites and apps that look good and are hard to break. Outside of class, I'm always improving my projects, customizing things to work exactly how I want, and exploring how AI works and how to get the most out of it.</p>
          <blockquote class="motto">I want to build software that feels finished.</blockquote>
          <p>I don't add technology to a project just because it is popular. Every tool should have a purpose, and the result should be clean code, thoughtful design and useful functionality.</p>
          <ul class="principles">
            <li><strong>Design</strong><span>Make it intuitive.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Code</strong><span>Make it maintainable.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Performance</strong><span>Make it fast.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Details</strong><span>Make it feel finished.</span></li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Education</h2>
          <ul class="principles">
            <li><strong>2026 to now</strong><span>Bachelor's degree in Cybersecurity, Universidad Tecnológica de Panamá.</span></li>
            <li><strong>2023 to 2025</strong><span>Specialized training in technology, English and values at Centro ¡Supérate! Fundación Alberto Motta.</span></li>
            <li><strong>2025</strong><span>High school diploma in science, Centro Educativo Guillermo Endara Galimany.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Languages</strong><span>Spanish, native. English, upper-intermediate (B2, TOEIC).</span></li>
          </ul>
          <p><a class="link-strong" href="experience.html">Full experience and certifications</a></p>
        </div>

